## Summary

In the desktop app, after switching away from a session and back a few times, the transcript can end up showing **only the user message** for the most recent turn — the assistant reply disappears from the UI even though the data is intact (it reappears after restarting Hermes). The user reports this has persisted across several versions.

## Reproduction

1. Start a turn in session A and **switch to session B while the assistant reply is still streaming** (or right as it completes).
2. Switch back to session A.
3. Repeat the A↔B switching a few times.
4. Eventually session A's transcript shows only the user message(s) for the recent turn — the assistant reply is not rendered, and nothing recovers it short of restarting the app (or occasionally switching away and back again).

## Root cause analysis

The bug lives in the resume/hydration reconciliation path (`apps/desktop/src/app/session/hooks/use-session-actions/utils.ts`).

When resuming a session, `reconcileAuthoritativeMessages` merges:
- `toChatMessages(authoritativeMessages)` — stored transcript (the streaming assistant row is **not** in the DB yet)
- `appendLiveSessionProjection(...)` — the backend `inflight` projection, which uses a **fixed id** `assistant-stream-${sessionId}`
- the local slice's live messages via `preserveLocalPendingTurnMessages`

The problem is in `preserveLocalPendingTurnMessages` (utils.ts:411-421):

```ts
const authoritative = nextByRoleOrdinal.get(`${message.role}:${ordinal}`)

if (authoritative) {
  if (isPendingAssistant) {
    continue  // ← authoritative assistant exists at the same ordinal → drop the LOCAL pending row unconditionally
  }
  ...
}
```

When the authoritative transcript already contains an assistant at the same role-ordinal (e.g. the projected `assistant-stream-${sessionId}` row, or a stored row), the **local pending assistant — which holds the full streamed content — is discarded unconditionally**, even when it is strictly more complete than the authoritative/projected copy. If the projected row has empty parts (e.g. `inflight.assistant` is empty when the turn just started streaming, or the turn finished right at switch time), the transcript ends up showing no assistant reply at all.

Because the streaming events have already stopped by then, nothing re-populates the missing row — the transcript stays broken until the app restarts and re-hydrates from the DB.

## Suggested fix

In `preserveLocalPendingTurnMessages` (apps/desktop/src/app/session/hooks/use-session-actions/utils.ts), when the local row is a pending assistant and an authoritative row exists at the same ordinal, **keep the more complete row** instead of unconditionally dropping the local one:

```ts
if (authoritative) {
  if (isPendingAssistant) {
    // Keep the local pending row when it has content the authoritative
    // row lacks (e.g. an empty inflight projection shell).
    const localText = chatMessageText(message).trim()
    const authoritativeText = chatMessageText(authoritative).trim()
    if (authoritativeText.length >= localText.length) {
      continue
    }
  } else {
    ...
  }
}
```

Related hardening that would help:
- `hydrateFromStoredSession` (apps/desktop/src/app/contrib/wiring.tsx): if the stored transcript is *shorter* than the local slice (local still has an in-flight turn), skip the overwrite.
- `shouldHydrate` in `use-message-stream` (apps/desktop/src/app/session/hooks/use-message-stream/index.ts): check whether the local slice still has an unfinished assistant before hydrating from storage on turn-complete.

## Environment

- Hermes v0.19.1 (also reproduced on earlier versions)
- Windows 10, desktop app
